<section id="faq" aria-labelledby="fq-title" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 id="fq-title">What Members and their offices ask</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Will I lose reach compared with the platforms I use now?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Your Rostrum account works in Bluesky and every other Atmosphere app from day one, where millions of people and many journalists are already active. You can cross-post to the networks you still use, and an open bridge carries your posts to Mastodon and the fediverse.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Do I have to leave the platforms I use now?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Most Members will run Rostrum alongside their existing accounts at first. Rostrum becomes the place you own, verified and portable, and the others become channels you publish to.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Is Rostrum an official EU service?</summary><div class="a"><p>No. Rostrum is proposed as an independent, not-for-profit service. It is not run, funded or endorsed by the European Parliament or any EU institution. It verifies Members using the Parliament's public register.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Is it really free?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes, for every Member and every political group. Rostrum is designed as public-interest infrastructure funded by foundations and grants. There are no ads, no paid reach and no data sales.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>I already have a Bluesky account. What happens to it?</summary><div class="a"><p>You can move it to Rostrum and keep your followers, posts and history. Your current handle can redirect to your new verified one, so nobody loses track of you.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Can I leave Rostrum and take my followers with me?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes. That's the point of the open social web: your account can move to any compatible provider, and your followers move with it.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Can my staff post for me?</summary><div class="a"><p>Yes, with the permissions you set. Every draft, approval and post records who did it, so accountability stays with the Member.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>How are citizens verified for polls and petitions?</summary><div class="a"><p>Taking part is open to everyone. Citizens who want their response counted as verified can prove residence in a member state with the EU Digital Identity Wallet, without sharing their name. Verified and open results are always shown separately.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What about national, regional and local representatives?</summary><div class="a"><p>Rostrum starts with Members of the European Parliament because the public register makes verification reliable. National, regional and local representatives follow in later phases.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
